# Unlike every 1-harness-sdk/* or 3-manual-instrumentation/* app, this
# folder has no main.py and no TRACE_TARGET switch -- docker-compose.yaml
# reads this file directly (both for its own ${VAR:-default}
# substitutions and, via env_file, as the litellm container's runtime
# environment). Local mode is the default: the file works as shipped,
# against mock-providers/'s stub server (start it first -- see README.md
# "Run"). To send traces to Harness Cloud & AI Cost Management instead,
# uncomment and fill in the three OTEL_* lines below.

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider (OpenAI, routed by config.yaml's model_list)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# There's no local-Ollama-style zero-cost path for this app the way
# 1-harness-sdk/openai/ has -- request.sh talks to the proxy over HTTP,
# and the proxy needs a real upstream to call. So this ships pointed at
# mock-providers/mock_openai_server.py by default instead -- start it on
# the host first (in a separate terminal, before `docker-compose up`):
#   uv run ../../mock-providers/mock_openai_server.py
# The mock ignores the key's value; the OpenAI-compatible client just
# requires a non-empty string. See mock-providers/README.md -- it's a
# canned response, not real model output, so switch to a real key below
# once you've confirmed a trace shows up in Jaeger.
OPENAI_API_KEY=mock-local-bypass-key

# host.docker.internal, not localhost/127.0.0.1: from inside the litellm
# container, that's the container's own loopback, not the host's --
# docker-compose.yaml's extra_hosts entry maps host.docker.internal to
# the host's real address for exactly this. Comment this line out (see
# config.yaml's comment on why leaving it out entirely, not setting it to
# an empty value, matters) to use a real OpenAI account instead.
OPENAI_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1

# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Harness (only needed to send traces to a real account instead of the
# bundled Jaeger -- uncomment all three)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxy-specific var (LLD §11.2), not the standard OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_*
# name -- LiteLLM is documented to fall back to the standard vars if this
# one is unset, but every app in this repo sets its family's native var
# explicitly rather than relying on a fallback path.
# OTEL_ENDPOINT=https://prod3.harness.io/udp-ingest/otel

# Same x-harness-service-token / x-tenant-id pair every app in this repo
# sends (see docs/01-get-your-token.md) -- an ordinary personal/service
# account token; tenant validation applies to it normally, same as any
# other credential.
# OTEL_HEADERS=x-harness-service-token=<TOKEN>,x-tenant-id=<ACCOUNT_ID>

# harness.account.id is required here the same way it is for every other
# app (see docs/01-get-your-token.md) -- keep service.name alongside it,
# not as two separate variables, since this is the one place both are set.
# OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=harness.account.id=<ACCOUNT_ID>,service.name=cacm-demo-litellm-proxy
